uire the new task equally prior to replay), but during replay C experiences retroactive competence loss on the new task (-0.50) due to back-interference from replaying old onset weights, explaining why strict empirical superiority across seeds was 0.0%. The holdout evaluation measures Property A (retention of shared phonetic-orthographic transitions across isolated lexical records) rather than full lexical generalization to unseen words (Property C) or unseen transitions (Property B). Because this pilot evaluated 3 exploratory seeds on synthetic micro-fixtures, these results provide methodological validation of the protocol rather than definitive proof of general superiority across all linguistic contexts. The protocol is verified, reproducible, and ready for scaled execution on local CPU.
